{"uid":"d023eeb0fc7b0585","name":"TestKonvertSuite/TestFirstBootEVEKAppVolume","fullName":"github.com/lf-edge/eve/evetest/tests/konvert.TestKonvertSuite/TestFirstBootEVEKAppVolume","time":{"start":1795707173000,"stop":1795707625820,"duration":452820},"status":"passed","flaky":false,"newFailed":false,"newBroken":false,"newPassed":true,"retriesCount":0,"retriesStatusChange":false,"beforeStages":[],"testStage":{"steps":[],"attachments":[],"parameters":[],"hasContent":false,"shouldDisplayMessage":false,"stepsCount":0,"attachmentsCount":0,"attachmentStep":false},"afterStages":[],"labels":[{"name":"resultFormat","value":"junit"},{"name":"suite","value":"github.com/lf-edge/eve/evetest/tests/konvert"},{"name":"testClass","value":"github.com/lf-edge/eve/evetest/tests/konvert"},{"name":"package","value":"github.com/lf-edge/eve/evetest/tests/konvert"}],"parameters":[],"links":[],"hidden":false,"retry":false,"extra":{"severity":"normal","retries":[],"categories":[],"history":{"statistic":{"failed":3,"broken":0,"skipped":0,"passed":27,"unknown":0,"total":30},"items":[{"uid":"15dd0e284136908","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/56/#testresult/15dd0e284136908","status":"failed","statusDetails":"Device \"edge-dev\": expected 0 reboot(s) but observed 1\n\nClaude's conclusion:\nThis is a well-documented, recurring pillar bug, confirmed live. The device's `/persist`-recorded reboot-stack and my own log scrape of `gotest.json`/`evetest eve logs` show `zedbox` panicked with `panic: send on closed channel` at `pkg/pillar/cmd/downloader/download.go:473` inside the `objectMetadata` helper goroutine (`receiveChan <- nil`, spawned at line 468), while resolving the image tag `lfedge/evetest-ubuntu-ctr:1.0` for the deferred-volume app during `TestFirstBootEVEKAppVolume`'s \"deferred volume must now be created\" phase. The watchdog detected the crash and rebooted the device (restart counter 0→1 at 03:05:29), which is exactly the unexpected reboot `checkRebootCounts` flagged — the test's actual functional checkpoints (volume creation, app running) all completed successfully afterward.\n\nThis is the identical, already-diagnosed `receiveChan` close-vs-send race in `downloadHandler.create()`/`delete()` (`pkg/pillar/cmd/downloader/handlers.go`): the per-download-object channel is closed in `delete()` with no synchronization against an in-flight `objectMetadata` goroutine still writing to it. Per `live-ledger.md`, this exact panic/stack trace is a known, recurring issue first seen 2026-11-05, recurring 2026-11-08 and 2026-11-20 (all three times hitting `TestManyAppInterfaces`'s concurrent-download burst) — tonight is the first time it's hit `TestFirstBootEVEKAppVolume` instead, triggered by the same race under a different concurrent-download workload (image resolve for the deferred-volume app), not a new bug. This does not share a root cause with any other failure already in tonight's run.","time":{"start":1795652772000,"stop":1795653749990,"duration":977990}},{"uid":"e11ed7da4230966a","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/51/#testresult/e11ed7da4230966a","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795566038000,"stop":1795566467670,"duration":429670}},{"uid":"af7b67fd30089edf","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/46/#testresult/af7b67fd30089edf","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795471355000,"stop":1795471810580,"duration":455580}},{"uid":"165ad4bccc1d0f50","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/41/#testresult/165ad4bccc1d0f50","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795398602000,"stop":1795399050390,"duration":448390}},{"uid":"713986915ff95eb9","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/36/#testresult/713986915ff95eb9","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795298541000,"stop":1795298983190,"duration":442190}},{"uid":"2bd87983384c74d0","reportUrl":"https://lf-edge.github.io/eve/test/master/runs/31/#testresult/2bd87983384c74d0","status":"passed","time":{"start":1795220716